    row
      col
        h1 Button
        h2 The classic button, in different colors, sizes, and states
      col
        card
          link "https://srv.carbonads.net/ads/click/x/GTND4277CVBD6KQICVYLYKQUF67ITKJLC6SDTZ3JCAAI653UCVBI523KCKBI62QNCE7IP53LF6BIC5QJFTBI42JKC6SILKJWCYADEK3EHJNCLSIZ" https://srv.carbonads.net/ads/click/x/GTND4277CVBD6KQICVYLYKQUF67ITKJLC6SDTZ3JCAAI653UCVBI523KCKBI62QNCE7IP53LF6BIC5QJFTBI42JKC6SILKJWCYADEK3EHJNCLSIZ
          link "One SDK. Any model. Ship agents. Get started." https://srv.carbonads.net/ads/click/x/GTND4277CVBD6KQICVYLYKQUF67ITKJLC6SDTZ3JCAAI653UCVBI523KCKBI62QNCE7IP53LF6BIC5QJFTBI42JKC6SILKJWCYADEK3EHJNCLSIZ
        link "ads via Carbon" http://carbonads.net/?utm_source=bulmaio&utm_medium=ad_via_link&utm_campaign=in_unit&utm_term=carbon
    text The button is an essential element of any design. It's meant to look and behave as an interactive element of your page.
    text Example
    button Button
    text HTML
    text "<button class=\"button\">Button</button>"
    button Copy danger
    text The button class can be used on:
    text <a> anchor links
    text <button> form buttons
    text "<input type=\"submit\"> submit inputs"
    text "<input type=\"reset\"> reset inputs"
    text Example
    row
      button Button
      button button
      button button
    text HTML
    text "<a class=\"button\">Anchor</a> <button class=\"button\">Button</button> <input class=\"button\" type=\"submit\" value=\"Submit input\" /> <input class=\"button\" type=\"reset\" value=\"Reset input\" />"
    button Copy danger
    h3 "Colors #"
    row
      text different colors
      link "$colors Sass map" #
    text Example
    row
      button White
      button Light
      button Dark primary
      button Black primary
      button Text
      button Ghost
    text HTML
    text "<button class=\"button is-white\">White</button> <button class=\"button is-light\">Light</button> <button class=\"button is-dark\">Dark</button> <button class=\"button is-black\">Black</button> <button class=\"button is-text\">Text</button> <button class=\"button is-ghost\">Ghost</button>"
    button Copy danger
    text Example
    row
      button Primary success
      button Link primary
    row
      button Info primary
      button Success success
      button Warning warning
      button Danger danger
    text HTML
    text "<div class=\"buttons\"> <button class=\"button is-primary\">Primary</button> <button class=\"button is-link\">Link</button> </div> <div class=\"buttons\"> <button class=\"button is-info\">Info</button> <button class=\"button is-success\">Success</button> <button class=\"button is-warning\">Warning</button> <button class=\"button is-danger\">Danger</button> </div>"
    button Copy danger
    text Each color also comes in its light version. Simply append the modifier is-light to the color modifier to apply the light version of the button.
    text Example
    row
      button Primary
      button Link
    row
      button Info
      button Success
      button Warning
      button Danger
    text HTML
    text "<div class=\"buttons\"> <button class=\"button is-primary is-light\">Primary</button> <button class=\"button is-link is-light\">Link</button> </div> <div class=\"buttons\"> <button class=\"button is-info is-light\">Info</button> <button class=\"button is-success is-light\">Success</button> <button class=\"button is-warning is-light\">Warning</button> <button class=\"button is-danger is-light\">Danger</button> </div>"
    button Copy danger
    text A dark version also exists. Simply append the modifier is-dark.
    text Example
    row
      button Primary success
      button Link primary
    row
      button Info primary
      button Success primary
      button Warning warning
      button Danger danger
    text HTML
    text "<div class=\"buttons\"> <button class=\"button is-primary is-dark\">Primary</button> <button class=\"button is-link is-dark\">Link</button> </div> <div class=\"buttons\"> <button class=\"button is-info is-dark\">Info</button> <button class=\"button is-success is-dark\">Success</button> <button class=\"button is-warning is-dark\">Warning</button> <button class=\"button is-danger is-dark\">Danger</button> </div>"
    button Copy danger
    h3 "Sizes #"
    text The button comes in 4 different sizes:
    text small
    text normal
    text medium
    text large
    text While the default size is the normal one, the is-normal modifier exists in case you need to reset the button to its normal size.
    text Example
    row
      button Small
      button Default
      button Normal
      button Medium
      button Large
    text HTML
    text "<button class=\"button is-small\">Small</button> <button class=\"button\">Default</button> <button class=\"button is-normal\">Normal</button> <button class=\"button is-medium\">Medium</button> <button class=\"button is-large\">Large</button>"
    button Copy danger
    text You can change the size of multiple buttons at once by wrapping them in a buttons parent, and applying one of 3 modifiers:
    text buttons are-small
    text buttons are-medium
    text buttons are-large
    text Example
    row
      button All
      button Medium
      button Size
    text HTML
    text "<div class=\"buttons are-medium\"> <button class=\"button\">All</button> <button class=\"button\">Medium</button> <button class=\"button\">Size</button> </div>"
    button Copy danger
    text You can change the size of only a subset of buttons by simply applying a modifier class to them. For example, if you want all buttons to be small but still have one in its normal size, simply do the following:
    text Example
    row
      button Small
      button Small
      button Small
      button Normal
      button Small
    text HTML
    text "<div class=\"buttons are-small\"> <button class=\"button\">Small</button> <button class=\"button\">Small</button> <button class=\"button\">Small</button> <button class=\"button is-normal\">Normal</button> <button class=\"button\">Small</button> </div>"
    button Copy danger
    h3 "Responsive sizes #"
    text If you want different button sizes for each breakpoint, you can use Bulma's responsive buttons. Simply append the is-responsive modifier:
    table Name Fixed Responsive Code:badge
      Default | Default | Default | <button class="button is-responsive"> Default </button>Copy
      Small | Small | Small | <button class="button is-small is-responsive"> Small </button>Copy
      Normal | Normal | Normal | <button class="button is-normal is-responsive"> Normal </button>Copy
      Medium | Medium | Medium | <button class="button is-medium is-responsive"> Medium </button>Copy
      Large | Large | Large | <button class="button is-large is-responsive"> Large </button>Copy
    text You can customise the sizes by overwriting the $button-responsive-sizes Sass variable.
    h3 "Displays #"
    text Example
    row
      button Small
      button Normal
      button Medium
      button Large
    text HTML
    text "<button class=\"button is-small is-fullwidth\">Small</button> <button class=\"button is-fullwidth\">Normal</button> <button class=\"button is-medium is-fullwidth\">Medium</button> <button class=\"button is-large is-fullwidth\">Large</button>"
    button Copy danger
    h3 "Styles #"
    h3 Outlined
    text Example
    row
      button Outlined
      button Outlined
      button Outlined
      button Outlined
      button Outlined
    text HTML
    text "<button class=\"button is-link is-outlined\">Outlined</button> <button class=\"button is-primary is-outlined\">Outlined</button> <button class=\"button is-info is-outlined\">Outlined</button> <button class=\"button is-success is-outlined\">Outlined</button> <button class=\"button is-danger is-outlined\">Outlined</button>"
    button Copy danger
